{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe specialist's completed investigation found no diagnosable cause for a single confirmed blackout, and the signed chronology documents one event with no further events over 3.8 years; the nurse records that this is a blackout of undetermined nature after investigation, rather than an investigation still pending, while an earlier faint in the driver's father is kept separate from the patient's event count and cannot create a recurrent patient history.\n\nThe employer's copied form relates to an earlier period of work and contains a broad satisfactory box without the measurements underlying it, whereas the current nurse entry identifies the source of each specific finding; the driver's wish to continue scheduled duties is recorded as a preference, not as proof that the present assessment has resolved the documented concern.\n\nThe nurse reads the summary back to the driver to check the chronology and separates agreement about the wording from verification of a medical finding, then attaches the identified clinical material; any decision about further investigation or work allocation remains for the reviewing professional, and the note itself does not certify that all relevant clinical questions have been answered.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
